1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Now the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the son of Amittai, saying, Arise, go to Nineveh, that great city, and cry against it; for their wickedness is come up before me. But Jonah rose up to flee unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD, and went down to Joppa; and he found a ship going to Tarshish: so he paid the fare thereof, and went down into it, to go with them unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD.

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Yahweh told Jonah to go to Nineveh. Look which way Jonah is going! That is the wrong way.

3
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:54.000
But the LORD sent out a great wind into the sea, and there was a mighty tempest in the sea, so that the ship was like to be broken.

4
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Hold on tight! Yahweh sent a great wind, and the sailors were afraid.

5
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Now the LORD had prepared a great fish to swallow up Jonah. And Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights.

6
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Three days inside a fish! Yahweh had a plan for Jonah even there.

7
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Then Jonah prayed unto the LORD his God out of the fish’s belly,

8
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Even inside the fish, Jonah could pray. Yahweh hears us anywhere.

9
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:54.000
And the LORD spake unto the fish, and it vomited out Jonah upon the dry land.

10
00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Safe on dry land! Yahweh told the fish what to do, and it did.

11
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:34.000
And the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the second time, saying, Arise, go unto Nineveh, that great city, and preach unto it the preaching that I bid thee. So Jonah arose, and went unto Nineveh, according to the word of the LORD. Now Nineveh was an exceeding great city of three days’ journey.

12
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
This time Jonah went the right way. Nineveh was a very big city.

13
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:14.000
So the people of Nineveh believed God, and proclaimed a fast, and put on sackcloth, from the greatest of them even to the least of them.

14
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.000
The people listened and believed God. Even the king put on rough clothes to show he was sorry.

15
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:54.000
And God saw their works, that they turned from their evil way; and God repented of the evil, that he had said that he would do unto them; and he did it not.

16
00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Yahweh saw that they turned from doing wrong, and He showed them mercy. He is kind!
